{"type":"message","id":"d6d4defc","parentId":"72ddfcf0","timestamp":"2026-10-17T22:49:25.316Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`test_dates` now passes. The cause was the format string `\"%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S\"`: it doesn't allow the trailing `Z`, so `strptime` stopped there and raised.\n\nThe fix, in `dates/parse.py`, replaces the `strptime` call with `datetime.fromisoformat(s)`. On Python 3.11 and later (this environment runs 3.13.5), that reads both `...Z` and timestamps without a timezone. All 3 tests in `tests/test_parse.py` pass.\n\n**Behaviour change:**\n- **Input with `Z` or an offset:** `parse_date` now returns a datetime that carries its timezone. Comparing it with or subtracting it from a datetime that has no timezone raises `TypeError`. Callers that mix the two would need to make them consistent.\n- **Input without a timezone:** you still get a datetime with no timezone, as before.\n- **Other ISO-8601 forms:** inputs like a bare date (`2026-10-12`) or fractional seconds are now also accepted."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":351,"cacheRead":25496,"cacheWrite":1242,"totalTokens":27091,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":1242}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792277360787,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011Cg8dFDpt71i6AM6bR19fz","duration":4517.837041999999,"ttft":4499.597802,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":26740,"nonMessageTokens":21589,"compactionEpoch":0}}}
